          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.14.21"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kings 14.21",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ",",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.14.22"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "22",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.15.2"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "15.2",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ",",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.15.3"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "3",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And all the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amaziah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He built Eloth and restored it to Judah, after the king slept with his fathers. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Uzziah was sixteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-two years in Jerusalem. His mother's name was Jecoliah of Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he did what was right in the eyes of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", according to all that his father Amaziah had done. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He set himself to seek God in the days of Zechariah, who instructed him in the fear of God; and as long as he sought the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", God made him prosper.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He went out and made war against the Philistines, and broke down the wall of Gath and the wall of Jabneh and the wall of Ashdod; and he built cities in the territory of Ashdod and elsewhere among the Philistines. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "God helped him against the Philistines, and against the Arabs that dwelt in Gurbaal, and against the Me-unites. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Ammonites paid tribute to Uzziah, and his fame spread even to the border of Egypt, for he became very strong. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moreover Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the Corner Gate and at the Valley Gate and at the Angle, and fortified them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he built towers in the wilderness, and hewed out many cisterns, for he had large herds, both in the Shephelah and in the plain, and he had farmers and vinedressers in the hills and in the fertile lands, for he loved the soil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moreover Uzziah had an army of soldiers, fit for war, in divisions according to the numbers in the muster made by Je-iel the secretary and Ma-aseiah the officer, under the direction of Hananiah, one of the king's commanders. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The whole number of the heads of fathers' houses of mighty men of valor was two thousand six hundred. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Under their command was an army of three hundred and seven thousand five hundred, who could make war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Uzziah prepared for all the army shields, spears, helmets, coats of mail, bows, and stones for slinging. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In Jerusalem he made engines, invented by skilful men, to be on the towers and the corners, to shoot arrows and great stones. And his fame spread far, for he was marvelously helped, till he was strong.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when he was strong he grew proud, to his destruction. For he was false to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " his God, and entered the temple of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " to burn incense on the altar of incense. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Azariah the priest went in after him, with eighty priests of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " who were men of valor; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and they withstood King Uzziah, and said to him, “It is not for you, Uzziah, to burn incense to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", but for the priests the sons of Aaron, who are consecrated to burn incense. Go out of the sanctuary; for you have done wrong, and it will bring you no honor from the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " God.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Uzziah was angry. Now he had a censer in his hand to burn incense, and when he became angry with the priests leprosy broke out on his forehead, in the presence of the priests in the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", by the altar of incense. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.15.5+2KI.15.6+2KI.15.7"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kings 15.5-7",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And Azariah the chief priest, and all the priests, looked at him, and behold, he was leprous in his forehead! And they thrust him out quickly, and he himself hastened to go out, because the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had smitten him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And King Uzziah was a leper to the day of his death, and being a leper dwelt in a separate house, for he was excluded from the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". And Jotham his son was over the king's household, governing the people of the land.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah, from first to last, Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz wrote. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 26:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Uzziah slept with his fathers, and they buried him with his fathers in the burial field which belonged to the kings, for they said, “He is a leper.” And Jotham his son reigned in his stead.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.26.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.26.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
